<Base lang="en" title="UP Scholarship 2026-27: November Verification Schedule — What Happens When" description="The November verification dates for UP Scholarship 2026-27 Dashmottar fresh and renewal applications — NIC scrutiny, university verification, the correction window and the full payment list." path="/en/blog/up-scholarship-verification-november-2026/" altPath="/blog/up-scholarship-verification-november-2026/" faqs={faqs} updated="6 November 2026" datePublished="2026-11-06" dateModified="2026-11-06">
<div class="content-col"><h1 class="page-title">UP Scholarship 2026-27: the November verification schedule</h1>
<p class="note">Note: This is an independent information guide — it is not the official portal (edistrict.up.gov.in).</p>
<p class="updated-line">As per the official schedule (scholarship.up.gov.in) · November 2026</p>
<figure class="blog-featured"><img src="/images/blog/up-scholarship-verification-november-2026-featured.webp" alt="UP Scholarship 2026-27 verification schedule for November 2026 (example illustration)" /><figcaption>Example illustration • Illustration — edistrictupseva.com</figcaption></figure>
<section class="box"><h2>What is happening in November</h2><p>October was for filling forms — November is the month of verification. Here is the last date for every task:</p><table class="data"><thead><tr><th>Task</th><th>Who</th><th>By when</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Institution verification and forwarding</td><td>Dashmottar Fresh</td><td>10 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>University / affiliating body verification</td><td>Dashmottar Fresh</td><td>25 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>NIC scrutiny</td><td>Dashmottar Renewal</td><td>6–20 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>University verification</td><td>Dashmottar Renewal</td><td>5 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>NIC scrutiny</td><td>Pre / Post-Matric Fresh</td><td>6–15 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Correction window</td><td>Dashmottar Renewal + Inter</td><td>21 November–20 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Correction window</td><td>Dashmottar Fresh</td><td>16 December 2026–10 January 2027</td></tr><tr><td>First phase of payment (PFMS)</td><td>—</td><td>21–31 December 2026</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note">Dates are as per the official schedule — scholarship.up.gov.in is final for any change.</div></section>
<figure class="shot"><img src="/images/blog/scholarship-timeline.svg" alt="UP Scholarship November 2026 verification timeline" /><figcaption>November 2026 verification timeline — edistrictupseva.com</figcaption></figure>
<section class="box"><h2>Three categories — different dates</h2><p>UP Scholarship is not one scheme — there are three separate categories, and each has its own schedule:</p><ul><li><strong>Pre-Matric (Class 9–10):</strong> For younger students. Verification of fresh applications by the District School Inspector (DIOS) was due by 5 November 2026, and NIC scrutiny runs 6–15 November 2026.</li><li><strong>Post-Matric Inter (Class 11–12):</strong> For Intermediate students. Their correction window runs with Dashmottar Renewal, 21 November–20 December 2026.</li><li><strong>Dashmottar (Post-Matric, after Class 12):</strong> For degree, diploma, ITI and B.Ed courses — this is the largest category. Fresh applications were accepted until 31 October 2026 and renewals until 15 October 2026.</li></ul><p>Identify your category — it is better to follow the schedule for the category written on your form than to worry over another category’s dates.</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Verification stages — step by step</h2><p>After you submit the form, your application passes through these stages:</p><ol><li><strong>Institution verification:</strong> Your college or school checks the form and forwards it — for Dashmottar Fresh this is due by 10 November 2026. If your college has not forwarded it yet, contact the college immediately.</li><li><strong>University / DIOS verification:</strong> The university or district officer verifies genuine students and blocks wrong applications.</li><li><strong>NIC scrutiny:</strong> The National Informatics Centre checks the data — 6–20 November for Renewal and 26 November–5 December 2026 for Fresh.</li><li><strong>Data lock and demand creation:</strong> For Renewal, data lock is 21–26 November and demand creation is 27–30 November 2026 — after this, payment preparation begins.</li><li><strong>Payment (PFMS):</strong> The first phase of payment is due between 21–31 December 2026, through PFMS by DBT into an Aadhaar-linked bank account.</li></ol><p>For fresh applications, rectification of suspicious or wrong data takes place between 6–31 December 2026.</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>What to do if verification is stuck</h2><p>If your status has been stuck at the same stage for a long time, first ask your college or school whether the form was forwarded — for Dashmottar Fresh, the last date for institution verification is 10 November 2026. After that, contact the university or affiliating body. At the NIC scrutiny stage you do not have to do anything, but if the status shows “suspicious data” or verification failed, wait for the correction window and note your category’s dates — once the window closes, there is no chance to fix a mistake.</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>How to check status and payment</h2><p>Two different places have to be checked — the form’s status and the payment’s status are separate:</p><ul><li><strong>Form status:</strong> Open “Status” on scholarship.up.gov.in and check with your application number — it shows the verification stage.</li><li><strong>Payment status:</strong> Check on the PFMS portal (pfms.nic.in) under “Know Your Payment” — you need the bank’s name and the account number.</li><li><strong>Ask your college:</strong> District verification ran between 16 October–5 November 2026 — if the institute did not forward the form, the status will not move ahead, so confirm with the college.</li></ul></section>
<section class="box"><h2>If Aadhaar verification has failed</h2><p>If your form shows “Aadhaar Demographic Verification Failed”, do not panic — it usually happens because of a mistake in the name, father’s or mother’s name, date of birth, category, marks, income or bank account. All of these can be corrected in the official Correction window — see your category’s window in the table above. If the Aadhaar record is correct, fix the form; if the form is correct, get the Aadhaar record fixed. Once the window closes, there is no chance to correct it, so do not miss the dates.</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>How the payment arrives</h2><p>The scholarship amount comes directly by DBT into your <strong>Aadhaar-linked bank account</strong> — there is no agent in between. So make two things certain in advance: the bank account is linked to Aadhaar, and the account number written in the form is correct. If the account is not linked to Aadhaar, the payment can get stuck — visit the bank and get Aadhaar seeding done. The first phase of payment is scheduled for 21–31 December 2026, and payment for Class 9–12 renewal students had already started between 25–31 October 2026.</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>The income certificate link</h2><p>An income certificate is needed for the scholarship — if yours is not made yet or has become old, see the documents and process in the <a href="/en/income-certificate/">Income Certificate guide</a>. An income certificate is usually valid for 3 years, but the scholarship needs fresh income details — the income written in the form and the income on the certificate should not differ, otherwise verification gets stuck.</p></section></div></Base>
